    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r7:t5",
    "narration": "The observation floor caught the afternoon light through its narrow windows, the stone walls holding a cool stillness that made the quiet feel deliberate rather than empty. The two unused beds sat bare at the room's center, flanked by their stools and nightstands and the tall empty wardrobes. Beyond them, the wooden medical-storage cabinets stood shut and hollow. Nothing here was in use; the space merely waited.\n\nIris was quiet for a moment after the question. She sat on one of the stools, her gaze drifting toward the windows before settling.\n\n\"I don't need much,\" Iris said. \"This is enough. Sitting somewhere that isn't loud.\" She paused, then added, \"If something needs doing, I can do it.\"",
